# A copy of a station permanent copies its printed abilities, the striations included, but not its counters: "The abilities
# (and in some cases, types, power, and toughness) are determined based on the number of charge counters on the copy" (Wurmwall
# Sweeper's rulings, 2025-07-25; CR 707.2). The Sweeper, stationed to four by Sunset Saboteur on turn 1, is a 2/2 flying
# artifact creature; Phyrexian Metamorph entering as a copy of it on turn 3 has no counters and is only an artifact (its
# copy surveils as it enters). The copy's own station ability, paid with the Saboteur, gives it four counters, and it is a
# 2/2 flier too - summoning sick, having entered this turn (CR 302.6).

